#: docs/guides/source-checkout.md:44
msgid ""
"Run these POSIX-shell commands from the parent directory containing the "
"downloaded manifest. Choose a new checkout directory; the commands do not "
"replace one that already exists. The Python command validates the identity "
"before passing it to Git:"
msgstr ""
"Run these POSIX-shell commands from the parent directory containing the "
"downloaded manifest. Choose a new checkout directory; the commands do not "
"replace one that already exists. The Python command validates the identity "
"before passing it to Git:"

#: docs/guides/source-checkout.md:62
msgid ""
"Check every command's exit status. `git rev-parse HEAD` must equal the "
"manifest's full commit. Recursive submodule lines must have neither a leading"
" `-` (missing), `+` (different revision) nor `U` (conflict), and `git status "
"--short` must be empty before starting a clean-source workflow. Stop on an "
"unavailable commit or failed dependency retrieval; never substitute `main`, "
"`HEAD` or a latest dependency. The preparation command audits the source-"
"owned catalogue and each parent Gitlink before initializing its explicitly "
"selected paths. Firmware configuration does not retrieve dependencies. For "
"historical revisions predating this command, use the matching immutable "
"documentation rather than applying current commands to an older source tree. "
"For a preview without a package manifest, record the full commit from its "
"source banner or `documentation-build.json` and use that validated commit "
"explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Check every command's exit status. `git rev-parse HEAD` must equal the "
"manifest's full commit. Recursive submodule lines must have neither a leading"
" `-` (missing), `+` (different revision) nor `U` (conflict), and `git status "
"--short` must be empty before starting a clean-source workflow. Stop on an "
"unavailable commit or failed dependency retrieval; never substitute `main`, "
"`HEAD` or a latest dependency. The preparation command audits the source-"
"owned catalogue and each parent Gitlink before initializing its explicitly "
"selected paths. Firmware configuration does not retrieve dependencies. For "
"historical revisions predating this command, use the matching immutable "
"documentation rather than applying current commands to an older source tree. "
"For a preview without a package manifest, record the full commit from its "
"source banner or `documentation-build.json` and use that validated commit "
"explicitly."

#: docs/guides/source-checkout.md:75
msgid ""
"Fetching the exact source commit avoids downloading unrelated artifact "
"branches. The `documentation-assets` branch holds large historical evidence "
"archives; it is not a source dependency. Retrieve only an archive identified "
"by the [software evidence entry](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/blob/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18/docs/status/software-"
"verification.md) when you need its original raw evidence. A verified Source "
"SDK is another supported consumption path; it does not require the source "
"repository's artifact history."
msgstr ""
"Fetching the exact source commit avoids downloading unrelated artifact "
"branches. The `documentation-assets` branch holds large historical evidence "
"archives; it is not a source dependency. Retrieve only an archive identified "
"by the [software evidence entry](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/blob/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18/docs/status/software-"
"verification.md) when you need its original raw evidence. A verified Source "
"SDK is another supported consumption path; it does not require the source "
"repository's artifact history."

#: docs/guides/source-checkout.md:82
msgid ""
"On Windows, run the POSIX snippet in Git Bash, or read the same manifest "
"field and perform the corresponding Git commands in your shell. Do not treat "
"the shell variable syntax as a portable PowerShell command."
msgstr ""
"On Windows, run the POSIX snippet in Git Bash, or read the same manifest "
"field and perform the corresponding Git commands in your shell. Do not treat "
"the shell variable syntax as a portable PowerShell command."

